(Two things compare field by field; a list or map field compares by its
 contents and a buffer field by its bytes.)
A thing called note has
  a text called title,
  a list called items,
  a map called counts,
  a buffer called body.

a note called first.
a note called second.
If first is second then, print "two new notes are equal".
append "eggs" to first's items.
If first is not second then, print "a list field differs".
append "eggs" to second's items.
Set first's counts's "k" to 1.
Set second's counts's "k" to 1.
append "text" to first's body.
append "text" to second's body.
If first is second then, print "equal fields again".
append "!" to second's body.
If first is not second then, print "a buffer field differs".
